\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Short-Term Forecast Horse Race. Difference in realized next-period real relative rent growth between forecasted high-growth and low-growth markets. Markets are ranked each period using rolling OLS forecasts based on individual predictors and selected combinations. Bars report average differences between the top and bottom quintiles (top panel) and top and bottom deciles (bottom panel). The RDI-based forecast (RDI plus lagged rent growth) outperforms all single-variable forecasts and a specification including vacancies, absorption, supply growth, and lagged rent growth jointly.}}{21}{figure.caption.17}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:short_term_forecast_horse_race}{{2}{21}{Short-Term Forecast Horse Race. Difference in realized next-period real relative rent growth between forecasted high-growth and low-growth markets. Markets are ranked each period using rolling OLS forecasts based on individual predictors and selected combinations. Bars report average differences between the top and bottom quintiles (top panel) and top and bottom deciles (bottom panel). The RDI-based forecast (RDI plus lagged rent growth) outperforms all single-variable forecasts and a specification including vacancies, absorption, supply growth, and lagged rent growth jointly}{figure.caption.17}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Average real relative rent growth over the subsequent five years for metropolitan areas grouped by the trailing five-year average sign of annual RDI changes. For comparison, the same sign-based grouping strategy is applied to vacancies, absorption, supply growth, and lagged rent growth. Persistent RDI changes generate stronger and more stable separation of future rent outcomes than alternative indicators.}}{22}{figure.caption.18}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:oos_density_delta_forecast}{{3}{22}{Average real relative rent growth over the subsequent five years for metropolitan areas grouped by the trailing five-year average sign of annual RDI changes. For comparison, the same sign-based grouping strategy is applied to vacancies, absorption, supply growth, and lagged rent growth. Persistent RDI changes generate stronger and more stable separation of future rent outcomes than alternative indicators}{figure.caption.18}{}}
